%% encode_star_equals_dagger_encode
%% decode_dagger_encode_returns_star
%% self_adjoint_residual_factor
%% self_adjoint_residual_reads_coefficient_difference
%% marked_E4_closed_formula
%% marked_original_scalar_decode
%% marked_dagger_reflection_equivariance
%% marked_scalar_read_without_division
%% marked_coefficient_reflection_equivariance
%% Sbit_matrix_involution
%% Tbit_matrix_involution
%% STbit_matrix_cube
%% Sbit_retained_coordinate_formula
%% Tbit_retained_coordinate_formula
%% Sbit_symbolic_translation_covariance
%% Tbit_symbolic_translation_covariance
%% Earlier modular polynomial checks (36) and rational boundary checks (15)
%% are historical checks on the preceding source revision. Their untouched
%% identities remain documented, but their old discharge total is not a claim
%% that every current obligation has been replayed after this refactoring.
%% The calibration/tree/path induction arguments and many analytic interface
%% obligations have written proofs or named sources, not fresh native receipts.
%% RH/GRH source branches remain exactly as labelled; none of the matrix or
%% chart identities alone asserts an original zero lies on the critical line.
%%
%% METAGRAPH REVISION: REPLAY AND CERTIFICATE SCOPE
%% The preceding receipt section is retained historical evidence. New source-only
%% receipts below concern the recovered CN/MG/TP elementary theorems. Exact symbolic
%% checks are separate from native Hets theorem discharge. Free-word, route,
%% natural-number and finite-list arguments use the written structural inductions.
%% The marked-zero view uses free-record generation and the exact original-matrix
%% section. No unproved marked-pair eta goal is promoted to a premise of a replay.
%% The general additive-defect proof is written next to its goals; the six native
%% attempts reached the 3-second bound. The tropical unequal-minimum proof and
%% finite-list leading-term induction are provided above. Their ATP status remains
%% distinct from those complete mathematical derivations and symbolic identities.
%%
%% Extract a Python or JSON section by removing its initial '%% ' from each line
%% strictly between the exact BEGIN_... and END_... marker lines. The three runnable
%% scripts below need only this Hets file; normalize_metagraph optionally accepts
%% the archived source graph for additional provenance. Example extraction:
%%   python3 -c "import pathlib,sys; s=pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text();
