%% SUBSTANTIVE SOURCE-READER FINDINGS AND FIXES
%% 1. In the first version, a following %implied annotation was inspected only
%%    on the label's current line. Moving it to the next line could incorrectly
%%    classify a goal as an axiom. The final annotation_status reads across
%%    whitespace. Intervening comments in this position are rejected rather
%%    than allowed to conceal a later annotation. Isolated atlas mutations
%%    confirmed rejection of both next-line and comment-hidden %implied cases.
%%
%% 2. Comparing the two renaming dictionaries alone did not establish their
%%    inherited theory domains. The final version checks the actual base names
%%    of MT26_CommutativeRing and PN25_Carrier and the complete required import
%%    path through the additive group, ring, matrices and PN/GT specifications.
%%    Isolated changes of a morphism base and a target's vector import were
%%    rejected. The actual two mappings compose H24Scalar->MT26_R->PN25Scalar,
%%    with the matching operation and vector/matrix renamings.
%%
%% 3. A fixed Python term signature initially required manual concordance with
%%    CASL declarations. The final source reader parses every accepted operation
%%    and free constructor declaration from the selected actual source blocks,
%%    applies the verified renamings, and checks every domain/codomain against
%%    SIG. Partial operations are not admitted in this equational fragment.
%%    Mutating the actual pn25U-family codomain was rejected.
%%
%% All three checks now operate on the one delivered atlas, rather than relying
%% on the existence or integrity of companion source fragments.
%%
%% KERNEL AND SOURCE-SCHEMA AUDIT
%% The admitted source dictionary contains 34 equation schemas. Each is read
%% from an actual labelled source axiom or an exact previously unnamed formula.
%% Conjunctive source clauses are projected to their explicitly indexed equation
%% components; their complete formula, component index and universal scope are
%% recorded. The restricted equation parser does not discard implication guards:
%% implications and other unsupported syntax fail parsing. All admitted schemas
%% have implied=false. The original target formulas have implied=true and are
%% stored in a separate target dictionary, never in the Inst whitelist.
%%
%% Terms are first-order typed ASTs. The checker reconstructs every application
%% from the fixed signature, rejects forged stored sorts, checks all arguments,
%% and prevents one free variable name from acquiring two sorts. Substitution
%% must supply exactly the used schema variables and preserve each variable's
%% sort. Since these are binder-free terms under recovered universal scopes,
%% the substitution is capture-free. All proof endpoints are compared by exact
%% typed syntax, not by algebraic normalization.
%%
%% Every primitive is checked independently:
%%   Refl: no children; both endpoints are the identical term.
%%   Sym: exactly one checked child; its endpoints are reversed.
%%   Trans: exactly two checked children; the middle terms are identical.
%%   Cong: exactly one checked child per operation argument, in order, with
%%         the declared argument sorts; both applications are reconstructed.
%%   Inst: no children; a source-only schema and complete explicit sorted
%%         substitution reconstruct the exact two endpoints.
%%
%% Child references must point to already checked nodes. A cycle or absent
%% child therefore cannot enter the checked equation table. Nodes have exact
%% field sets. The actual policy is checked against the built proof: identical
%% rule, equation, rule parameters, and COMPLETE ordered premise list. Its rank
%% is a natural number, is exactly zero for leaves or one plus maximum child
%% rank, and strictly decreases on every premise. A judgement has one selected
%% policy task. Every delivered node is reachable from a target or explicitly
%% listed generic cancellation anchor.
%%
%% The original four target labels and every conjunct are mandatory. Replacing
%% a root by a proof of another equation is rejected. The three generic
%% cancellation lemmas are themselves expanded to the five primitive rules.
%% There is no Lemma rule and neither their names nor target names are accepted
%% as Inst sources.
%%
%% The planner may compare its two constructed normal forms syntactically to
%% choose a final Trans/Sym plan, but the checker still validates every step
%% leading to those terms. As an independence check, Planner, ProofBuilder and
%% construct were replaced with functions that raise before calling check on
%% the serialized JSON. The valid proof still passed. The code invokes no
%% external prover or symbolic-algebra package in this path.
%%
%% EXECUTED REJECTION CHECKS
%% independent_review.py replayed the valid certificates and rejected twelve
%% targeted invalid variants:
%%   wrong-sort Inst substitution; target used as Inst source; derived lemma
%%   used as Inst source; omitted Cong argument; broken Trans midpoint;
%%   altered claimed endpoint; nondecreasing/understated policy rank; omitted
%%   policy child; cyclic proof reference; forged application sort; missing
%%   linearity conjunct; substituted target root.
%% Five source-reader regression mutations were also rejected, as described
%% above. Exact outcomes and final reviewed hashes are in independent_review.json.
%% These checks used isolated in-memory/copy mutations and changed no atlas or
%% delivered certificate. No additional E search was performed.
%%
%% EXACT ACTUAL PROOF CHARGES
%% The declared primitive charge is one for EACH Refl/Sym/Trans/Cong/Inst node.
%% For the expanded equation proof tree, T(v)=1+SUM T(child occurrence). The
%% review independently recomputed this using edge multiplicities mu: initialize
%% each declared root occurrence with one, propagate each parent's multiplicity
%% along EVERY ordered child occurrence, then T=SUM mu(v). This agrees with the
%% checker for every target. The source-instance counts below are a second,
%% separate observable charging only Inst nodes.
%%
%% Original goal                         DAG  expanded tree  DAG Inst  tree Inst
%% PN six-period involution               29             30        11         12
%% PN linearity, both conjuncts           89            125        34         51
%% PN six-channel matrix return           38             40        15         17
%% GT recipe equals PN normalizer         92             96        31         32
%% All four targets, shared union        237            291        82        112
%% Bundle plus 3 cancellation anchors    250            316        87        123
%%
%% The four target rows cannot be added to obtain shared DAG cost: their proofs
%% share nodes. Their expanded tree costs do add to 291. Conjunction packaging
%% is represented by requiring both checked equation roots; it is not an extra
%% unit-cost primitive in this explicitly stated model. The 250-node delivered
%% bundle includes thirteen generic anchor nodes outside the target-root union.
%%
%% The exact recurrence counts the constructed proof; it is not a shortest-proof
%% claim. A fixed H24 calibration valid for every competing admitted rule would
%% be needed to establish global minimality. The constructor's current policy
%% correctly states that it proves sound construction for these admitted tasks,
%% without such a minimum assertion. Source rule support, proof charge and
%% expanded/shared representation size are distinct quantities.
%%
