%% BEGIN_H24_DUAL_GATE_GUIDE
%% DG26 — CONSTRUCTIVE TWO-KERNEL H24 / BELNAP GATE
%% 25 November 2026. This continues the same Number_Theory_Torser_Atlas.het.
%%
%% RESULT
%%
%% The two-green protocol is constructively proved in independent Agda and
%% Lean developments. Python runs both native kernels on explicitly written
%% expected theorem types. The new development connects the actual recovered
%% H24 builder, signed evidence, original-context return, source-preserving
%% comorphisms, min-plus cost availability, and reversible physical control.
%%
%% Three statements have different types and are kept separate:
%%
%%   1. A finite operational admission decision is total.
%%   2. Admission yields the original proof/data under its retained context,
%%      provided either checked source decoder is sound.
%%   3. An entire proof-producing/checking job terminates with a paid bound
%%      when its displayed local progress and phase bounds are supplied.
%%
%% The new native replay establishes the structural theorems and the complete
%% finite controller. It does not instantiate every analytic hypothesis in
%% the earlier number-theory targets, a universal theorem-truth decider, or
%% an unrestricted polynomial-time producer for all mathematical sentences.
%% The original Robin/Lagarias/RH/GRH targets and their recorded premises are
%% preserved. They can use this protocol when their actual proof terms and
%% faithful source translations are supplied.
%%
%% 1. ONE SOURCE JUDGEMENT, TWO SIGNED EVIDENCE FIBRES
%%
%% Fix a source request q. Its identity includes the complete original goal,
%% the complete context, the frame, and the interpretation/checking protocol.
%% The native binding is a record of four finite bit strings; the protocol
%% string can encode its source-version data. The executable transport also
%% compares the source version as its own explicit JSON field.
%%
%% For checker i, let P_i(q) and N_i(q) be the types of positive and opposing
%% certificates for that exact request. An evidence record stores optional
%% inhabitants of BOTH types. Neither the absence of a positive certificate
%% nor a failed kernel process creates a member of N_i(q).
%%
%% The FOUR observation is e_i=(p_i,n_i), where each bit reports whether its
%% corresponding certificate entry is present:
%%
%%     00 unknown; 10 support only; 01 opposition only; 11 conflict.
%%
%% The gate is the finite Boolean function
%%
%%     G(e_1,e_2) = (p_1 AND p_2) AND NOT(n_1 OR n_2).
%%
%% Here NOT is Boolean negation of an evidence-presence bit. It is not an
%% inference that an unobserved source opposition is impossible. Belnap rail
%% negation exchanges support/opposition; it is a different operation.
%%
%% The truth meet of the two observations is
%%
%%     e_1 meet_t e_2 = (p_1 AND p_2, n_1 OR n_2).
%%
%% Therefore G tests whether that meet is support-only. The native exactness
%% theorem supplies both constructive directions:
%%
%%     G(e_1,e_2)=true  iff  e_1=(true,false) AND e_2=(true,false).
%%
%% Forward proof: split the Boolean conjunction. The first half forces both
%% positive bits. The second half forces the disjunction of the negative
%% bits to be false and hence forces each negative bit to be false. Reverse
%% proof: substitute the four returned equalities and reduce the definition.
%%
%% Evidence extraction performs dependent elimination on the actual optional
%% entries. An absent positive entry is incompatible with green; a present
%% entry yields its stored certificate. The returned record contains both
%% certificates, their stored-entry equations, and absence of recorded
%% opposition. Exact request comparisons transport each certificate into
%% P_i(q); they do not discard goal/context/frame/protocol differences.
%%
%% The Python signed ledger performs knowledge accumulation. Adding a new
%% support or opposition entry retains the other rail. Pending, failed and
%% timed-out observations leave every old entry unchanged. Permission can
%% be revoked when opposition arrives: 10 <=_k 11, but G(10,10)=true and
%% G(11,10)=false. Thus permission itself is not monotone in information.
%% This is the intended finite admission policy, not a claim that all FOUR
%% object-language connectives have that control behavior.
%%
%% 2. THE STRONGER ONE-SOUND-OF-TWO SOURCE RETURN
%%
%% Let H(q) be the retained hypotheses and C(q) the intended original proof
%% or returned-data type. A sound source decoder has the constructive type
%%
%%     S_i : (q : Request) -> P_i(q) -> H(q) -> C(q).
%%
%% After two green observations the gate has constructed c_1:P_1(q) and
%% c_2:P_2(q). Given a tagged choice S_1 + S_2, inspect the tag and return
%%
%%     S_1(q,c_1) : H(q)->C(q), or S_2(q,c_2) : H(q)->C(q).
%%
%% This proves that one sound decoder suffices once both approvals exist.
%% The theorem does not require a probabilistic independence premise. Agda
%% and Lean are distinct native implementations of the proof checks; neither
%% new proof is a second invocation of the other checker.
%%
%% Lean includes both a proposition-valued theorem and a Type-valued data
%% constructor. The latter takes a data-level Sum of decoders so that no
%% elimination from a logical existential into data, choice principle, or
%% proof-irrelevance identification is hidden in the result. Agda proves the
%% Type-valued statement with --safe --without-K. The required hypotheses
%% remain in the function type H(q)->C(q). Supplying H(q) applies the function;
%% having only a list of hypothesis names does not close the conclusion.
%%
%% The CASL presentation spells the source sequent out: the returned proof
%% is valid, has the exact original conclusion, and every assumption it uses
%% is allowed by the original context. Its decoder-soundness predicates are
%% defined conditions in the implication, not newly asserted universal facts.
%%
%% 3. THE ACTUAL H24 CONSTRUCTOR, MINIMA, AND CANONICITY
%%
%% The implementation imports the existing RHH24.build / Hilbert24Policy.build.
%% For a finitely branching rule system S and a supplied tight policy, build
%% selects its rule and recursively constructs every child at smaller rank.
%% The selected rule, the ordered complete premise family, and the original
%% judgement remain in the resulting Derivation S j. No alternate proof-tree
%% datatype or theorem oracle substitutes for the recovered constructor.
%%
%% The existing calibration law is
%%
%%     charge(r) + sum_i V(premise_i) = V(conclusion) + slack(r),
%%
%% with nonnegative slack. Induction telescopes it to
%%
%%     work(d) = V(j) + totalSlack(d).
%%
%% The ranked tight build has zero total slack, hence attains the lower bound
%% for every admitted competing derivation. These are native imported proof
%% terms, checked afresh in this replay. They concern the stated rule system
%% and its proof charge. Obtaining a policy for every raw mathematical goal,
%% and implementing it within a polynomial bit clock, are separate statements.
%%
%% For the same constructed p=build(policy,j), the two compilers form E_1(p)
%% and E_2(p). The new fixed-judgement acceptance theorem requires only the
%% successful checks of those two concrete compiled values. It assumes no
%% universal completeness theorem for every possible checker input. The
%% Agda ActualH24 integration likewise restricts acceptance and source-return
%% conditions to its actual built derivations.
%%
%% Canonicity comes from retained source round trips:
%%
%%     D_1(E_1(p)) = p = D_2(E_2(p)).
%%
%% The proof is the first return equation followed by the inverse of the
%% second. It applies to actual Source data, including the exact H24 tree.
%% Two different proofs of a common proposition, or two proofs with equal
%% minimum charge, need not be the same source witness. All tied minima from
%% the prior minimum-fibre construction remain available.
%%
%% For a source action a, define its target action on a retained encoding by
%%
%%     a_i = E_i o a o D_i.
%%
%% Then, using only D_i E_i=id on the source,
%%
%%     a_i(E_i(p)) = E_i(a(p)),
%%     D_i(a_i(E_i(p))) = a(p).
%%
%% These are checked pointwise naturality and source-return equations. A
%% target-side inverse E_i D_i=id is unnecessary on the retained image.
%% The prior full institution-comorphism and actual H24 rule-translation
%% proofs remain in the same file; these concrete two-compiler equations
%% reuse their source-return direction rather than declaring two whole
%% foundations automatically equivalent.
%%
%% 4. THE TRIPLE-ADJOINT AND TESSERACT READINGS
%%
%% Let I={first,second} and pi:I x Q -> Q. At a fixed request q the positive
%% certificate family has dependent product
%%
%%     (Pi_pi P)(q) = P_1(q) x P_2(q),
%%
%% while the negative family has dependent sum
%%
%%     (Sigma_pi N)(q) = N_1(q) + N_2(q).
%%
%% This is the finite-checker instance of the previously constructed signed
%% right pushforward (Pi positive, Sigma negative), inside
%% Sigma_pi |- pi* |- Pi_pi. The gate's returned certificate pair is the
%% positive dependent product; a certificate from either opposing summand
%% is sufficient to veto. Merely projecting away a checker is not a proof of
%% having obtained that dependent product.
%%
%% The earlier Beck--Chevalley and pointwise inverse results justify changing
%% the request/frame base while retaining these fibres. The new source-action
%% and retained-history equations implement the corresponding commuting
%% squares explicitly. No new global function extensionality axiom is needed.
%%
%% The two FOUR observations are precisely one vertex of the four-bit
%% tesseract. Permission is the indicator of vertex (1,0,1,0). For a changed
%% frame f, a transported reading must decode that frame: G_f(y)=G(y xor f),
%% so G_f(x xor f)=G(x). The fixed gate is not invariant under arbitrary
%% uninterpreted bit flips; its covariance uses the retained decoder, as in
%% the prior torser and comorphism proofs.
%%
%% 5. A MIN-PLUS CALCULATION THAT RETURNS THE SAME GATE
%%
%% Use the existing cost interpretation N union {infinity}, where infinity
%% is unavailable. Sequential composition adds finite costs; alternatives
%% take their minimum. Availability maps finite cost to true and infinity
%% to false. The independent native proofs construct
%%
%%     avail(a+b) = avail(a) AND avail(b),
%%     avail(min(a,b)) = avail(a) OR avail(b).
%%
%% Thus the two-checker approval cost pair is
%%
%%     (c_1+ + c_2+, min(c_1-,c_2-)).
%%
%% Projecting its availability gives exactly the truth-meet rails
%% (p_1 AND p_2, n_1 OR n_2), and testing support-only gives exactly G.
%% This derives the Boolean, FOUR and min-plus control calculations from one
%% specified approval operation. It is not the earlier signed-parity product
%% in TP26, whose positive component also receives a negative-negative term.
%%
%% The cost identities quantify over arbitrary natural costs by constructor
%% elimination. A finite number is not by itself a proof certificate. Any
%% interpretation as an attained minimum uses the existing H24 calibration
%% and actual certificate witnesses. These identities connect the controller
%% to the tropical cost layer without asserting an unsupported equivalence
%% of all analytic information with a valuation.
%%
%% 6. THE ACTUAL REVERSIBLE CONTROL CIRCUIT
%%
%% Wire order is
%%
%%     p1,n1,p2,n2,a,b,flag,one0,one1,left,right.
%%
%% The clean ancillas are a=b=false and one0=one1=true. The first nine gates
%% are the palindrome
%%
%%     T(one0,one1;n1), T(one0,one1;n2),
%%     T(p1,n1;a), T(p2,n2;b), T(a,b;flag),
%%     T(p2,n2;b), T(p1,n1;a),
%%     T(one0,one1;n2), T(one0,one1;n1).
%%
%% Here T(u,v;w) sends w to w xor (u AND v). The first two gates temporarily
%% complement the opposition bits; the last two restore them. The two local
%% green ancillas compute each p_i AND NOT n_i. The middle gate copies their
%% conjunction into the flag; reversal clears both temporary ancillas.
%%
%% Both native kernels establish
%%
%%     gate9(clean(e,flag)) = clean(e,flag xor G(e)),
%%     gate9(gate9(s)) = s for every nine-wire state s.
%%
%% To route an action, put one Fredkin controlled by flag between two copies
%% of gate9. This is an actual 18-Toffoli/one-Fredkin word, not an assumed
%% oracle for permission. Starting at flag=false it swaps the two action
%% ports exactly when G is true, returns flag=false, and retains all four
%% evidence bits, constants and clean ancillas. On arbitrary work-register
%% states the whole router is still an involution; the clean conditions are
%% needed specifically for its intended gate semantics.
%%
%% Python executes the primitive list and compares it with independent output
%% equations on all 512 nine-wire states, all 2048 eleven-wire states, all 32
%% clean oracle states and all 64 clean router states. It returns arbitrary
%% history by identity. The native history extension proves, pointwise,
%%
%%     R_H(s,h)=(R(s),h),
%%     R_K(s,k(h))=(id x k)(R_H(s,h)).
%%
%% On the clean six-bit basis (p1,n1,p2,n2,left,right), numbered from zero with
%% p1 most significant, the router fixes every basis index except 41 and 42,
%% which it exchanges. Hence its integer permutation matrix is
%%
%%     U=I-E(41,41)-E(42,42)+E(41,42)+E(42,41).
%%
%% Equivalently, for r=e_41-e_42, U=I-r r^T and r^T r=2. Multiplication gives
%% U^T=U and U^2=I. Over real/complex amplitudes this also gives U^dagger=U^-1.
%% The native statements prove the permutation-support transpose and the
%% pointwise amplitude return; the displayed matrix follows by linear extension.
%% These are exact reversible-state results, without an added spectral gap,
%% energy, dissipation, or proof-search-speed premise.
%%
%% The 9/19 counts are explicit construction counts. No global primitive-gate
%% minimality theorem is claimed. A local bit-machine clock additionally pays
%% wire addressing/routing and the implementation of its elementary gates.
%%
%% 7. CONSTRUCTIVE COMPLETION AND THE PAID CLOCK
%%
%% Let ready(s) be the actual stored, bound, two-green event. Let next(s) be
%% the next state, k(s) its paid cost and B(s) its nonnegative remaining credit.
%% For every state with ready(s)=false, require the local laws
%%
%%     1 <= k(s),
%%     k(s) + B(next(s)) <= B(s).
%%
%% They construct B(next(s)) < B(s). Recursion on B(s) therefore returns the
%% first ready state, together with an actual elapsed time t and proofs
%%
%%     t <= B(s0),
%%     ready(run(s0,t))=true,
%%     sum of the t executed costs <= B(s0).
%%
%% At B=0 an unfinished step is impossible because its positive cost would
%% exceed the available credit. At a larger B the recursive result is lifted
%% one step and the paid inequality is composed. This is a proof-derived
%% finite computation, not a timeout being treated as a mathematical answer.
%%
%% Agda explicitly instantiates ready with boundGo and returns the original
%% proof/data at the constructed stopping state. The ActualH24.PaidJob clock
%% starts after build has formed its source derivation. Producer construction
%% time is therefore separately present in the complete phase ledger:
%%
%%     producer + compile1 + compile2 + check1 + check2
%%       + source-return + communication + physical-control.
%%
%% Both native kernels prove monotonicity of this sum. Given actual bounds
%% c_i(n) <= a_i (n+1)^d on the original input length for every phase, they
%% prove sum_i c_i(n) <= (sum_i a_i)(n+1)^d by arithmetic induction and
%% substitution. This composes supplied polynomial bounds; it does not supply
%% an absent bound for proof discovery, output expansion, checking or routing.
%% The prior physical-clock theorem also retains the positive cost of reversal:
%% returning to the original state by compute/uncompute pays c+c.
%%
%% There is a constructive countermodel to deriving termination from safety
%% alone: both certificate types may be Empty and both sound decoders then
%% exist by empty elimination, while both evidence streams remain Unknown at
%% every time. No green event occurs. That loop cannot satisfy the displayed
%% positive paid-progress laws. This identifies the additional theorem a
%% particular proposed total H24 process must establish.
%%
%% 8. WHAT THE EXECUTABLE REPLAY DOES
%%
%% The frozen challenge contains 23 native sources: 11 Agda and 12 Lean.
%% The expected signatures are written explicitly, rather than inferred from
%% the theorem whose name is being accepted. The full combined Agda entry
%% checks every imported source with safe/without-K/double-check, ignoring
%% interfaces. The Lean imports are rebuilt from source into a fresh private
%% compiled-module directory, with every required axiom report checked empty.
%% The Python runner checks complete source bytes and complete request bytes.
%%
%% Source bytes are read once, hashed, and copied to private per-kernel work
%% directories before checking. Thus later edits in the shared workspace do
%% not change the goal or proof used by an already started run. Empty build
%% lists, missing typed declarations, escaping source/include paths and a
%% missing required axiom report prevent acceptance. Hashes bind the reviewed
%% bytes; semantic source correspondence is provided by the displayed types,
%% definitions and explicit comorphism/decoder laws, not by a hash alone.
%%
%% The native signed table independently decides every one of the sixteen
%% concrete propositions G(e)=true. One has a positive proof; fifteen have
%% constructive refutations P->False. The Python ledger records their actual
%% named checked declarations with their positive/opposition roles. It also
%% checks that failure leaves those entries present. Separate deliberately
%% false proof submissions are rejected by both kernels and remain Unknown;
%% their rejection is not substituted for a checked refutation.
%%
%% The four-rail model covers conflicting observations. This run does not
%% fabricate mutually inconsistent classical native certificates for a single
%% Boolean proposition. The generic independent signed types still represent
%% Both without an explosion rule, as proved by the native Unit/Unit example.
%%
%% The 139 named Lean axiom reports include reused foundation theorems,
%% expected-type wrappers, and the sixteen signed instances; they are not a
%% claim of 139 new discoveries. All successful native receipts are embedded.
%% Agda introduces no postulates or holes in the safe dependency closure.
%% These remain proofs inside their explicit trusted type theories; there is
%% no claim of absolute foundation-free metatheoretic soundness.
%%
%% Hets parses and statically analyses the combined CASL development. Its
%% %implied declarations are proof obligations; the embedded Agda/Lean source
%% terms are the new constructive evidence. This addition does not claim a
%% generic verified Agda/Lean-to-CASL elaborator, nor an extra Hets ATP proof
%% for every old or new obligation. Each presentation's precise scope remains
%% visible in its signatures and receipts.
%%
%% 9. SINGLE-FILE REUSE AND SOURCES
%%
%% Read BEGIN_H24_DUAL_GATE_MANIFEST_JSON for the current receipt. Extract the
%% small Python block BEGIN_H24_DUAL_GATE_EXTRACT_PY, stripping the leading
%% CASL comment markers, and run:
%%
%%     python extract_dual_gate.py Number_Theory_Torser_Atlas.het extracted
%%     python extracted/dual_gate.py --agda /path/to/agda --lean /path/to/lean
%%
%% The native executables are external installed proof runtimes. All new proof
%% sources, expected types, signed instances, source manifest, Python runner,
%% reversible circuit and receipts are contained in this one Hets file.
%% Identical native contents are stored once; canonical Agda sources already
%% present in the prior contained archive are referenced by content hash.
%% The Boolean operations and FOUR carrier were factored into minimal shared
%% CASL specifications, so the gate itself requires no number-theory axioms.
%%
%% Primary contextual references, not substitutes for the contained proofs:
%%
%%   Belnap, A Useful Four-Valued Logic, 1977:
%%   https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-010-1161-7_2
%%   Lean reference, Validating a Lean Proof:
%%   https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/ValidatingProofs/
%%   Agda reference, Safe Agda:
%%   https://agda.readthedocs.io/en/latest/language/safe-agda.html
%%
%% No general RH/GRH status claim is added by this continuation. External
%% number-theory source receipts from the earlier version remain identified
%% as earlier receipts; this native run concerns the exact new structural
%% and controller statements described above.
%% END_H24_DUAL_GATE_GUIDE

