%% BEGIN_H24_UPLOADED_BRIDGE_GUIDE
%% CONSTRUCTIVE CLOCK, CHART AND INVOLUTION BRIDGE — 2026-11-25
%%
%% This continuation integrates the three uploaded files with the existing
%% Number_Theory_Torser_Atlas.het. It constructs and checks new proof terms in
%% Agda and Lean, composes them with the original two-green Belnap gate, and
%% reuses the atlas's existing source judgements, H24 constructor, matrix chart,
%% dagger normalizer, tesseract transports, comorphisms and family adjoints.
%%
%% One contained source package is sufficient to replay the new native batch.
%% It includes both unchanged Python uploads, the clock source proof modules,
%% the new independent proof modules, exact typed contracts, mathematical
%% derivations, receipts, and the unchanged two-kernel Python runner. Identical
%% contents are stored once or referenced by hash in prior contained archives.
%%
%% 1. WHAT IS CONSTRUCTED
%%
%% The main new composite is
%%
%%   local frontier balance + credit payment
%%     -> paid decreasing reserve
%%     -> actual original machine run / H24 HALT-TICK derivation
%%     -> the same bound two-green event
%%     -> both original certificates
%%     -> original claim under its retained source context.
%%
%% There is also a constructive converse:
%%
%%   halt within the SAME fixed budget
%%     -> finite boundedTicks on reached states
%%     -> decreasing reserve within that SAME budget.
%%
%% Both directions retain the machine, original start and budget. They do not
%% replace the source by a different formula or change its encoding length.
%% Agda constructs both maps at an arbitrary fixed budget function. Lean's
%% original uploaded records additionally carry coefficient and degree fields,
%% and prove that the converse preserves them. No reachability-witness choice,
%% function extensionality, UIP, or classical choice is needed in this path.
%%
%% The native batch uses Agda --safe --without-K --double-check, ignoring old
%% interfaces, and fresh Lean compiled imports. The unchanged runner requires
%% all requested Lean declarations to report empty added-axiom dependencies.
%% It compares the complete goal/context/frame/protocol/source request bytes,
%% then applies the original exact four-rail gate and reversible permission
%% router. Its result is recorded in replay/gate_receipt.json. Python performs
%% transport and process orchestration; it is not a third mathematical oracle.
%%
%% 2. FRONTIER TO ACTUAL PAID WORK
%%
%% For every live transition s -> t, let c(s)>=1 be its original paid cost and
%% let Phi, credit and a be natural-valued data. The local fields are
%%
%%   c(s) + Phi(t) = a(s,t) + Phi(s),
%%   a(s,t) + credit(t) <= credit(s).
%%
%% Set Psi(s)=Phi(s)+credit(s). Reassociate the first equation, substitute it,
%% and apply the second inequality:
%%
%%   c(s)+Psi(t)
%%     = Phi(s)+(a(s,t)+credit(t))
%%     <= Phi(s)+credit(s)=Psi(s).
%%
%% Thus every live transition consumes positive reserve. The constructive
%% finite-fuel recursion returns the first ready state, its actual history,
%% and both bounds
%%
%%   number_of_transitions <= actual_paid_work <= Psi(start).
%%
%% For the uploaded literal HALT/TICK grammar, c=1: HALT is arity zero with
%% charge zero and TICK has the actual next state as its sole premise and
%% charge one. A rank constructs remaining(s); remaining supplies a zero-slack
%% H24 calibration. The existing constructMinimum then returns a derivation,
%% and its decoder returns the same original execution, with
%%
%%   H24.work(proof) = ticks(decoded_execution) <= Psi(start).
%%
%% Its minimality is among derivations of this specified original grammar.
%% No search over competitor proofs is performed by this construction.
%%
%% The ready predicate in monitoredGatePlan is the actual boundGo of the two
%% certificate envelopes. Its halt-to-green property is proved from that
%% definition. The more general TerminalPlan needs the property only at
%% states reachable from the original start. This avoids requiring a semantic
%% condition about unrelated states.
%%
%% A machine State -> Option State is an explicit transition interface. Its
%% implementation as one primitive bit operation is additional concrete data.
%% If next executes a block of several primitive steps, the outer trace counts
%% blocks; PaidProgress separately bounds their supplied weighted costs. A
%% literal bit-clock result uses one-bit transitions or their paid microtrace
%% expansion. Host Python/kernel elapsed time is never substituted for this
%% cost model. Proof-production, conversion, checking, routing and readback
%% costs remain charged when they are executed.
%%
%% 3. THE SAME-DEADLINE CONVERSE
%%
%% Define by finite recursion
%%
%%   boundedTicks(0,s)=0,
%%   boundedTicks(n+1,s)=0                         if next(s)=none,
%%   boundedTicks(n+1,s)=1+boundedTicks(n,t)         if next(s)=some(t).
%%
%% It is always at most n. If runFor(n,s) has halted, one extra fuel unit
%% does not change boundedTicks. A state reached from a start which halts
%% within B also halts within B; no new deadline is chosen. Consequently
%%
%%   Psi_B(s)=boundedTicks(B,s)
%%
%% strictly decreases on every live reached edge, and Psi_B(start)<=B.
%% These are the reserve fields. Conversely, finite recursion on a decreasing
%% natural reserve constructs an Execution and proves it halts by B whenever
%% the initial reserve is <=B.
%%
%% Agda: H24ClockConverse.exact-clock-equivalence, its Uniform module, and
%% ClockBridgeContract. Lean: reserveFromDeadline, bridgeDeadline,
%% reserve_target_iff_deadline_target, converse_keeps_clock, and
%% H24ClockBridgeContract. The correspondence is between these constructive
%% mathematical maps; it is not an asserted equality of the two languages'
%% syntax or foundational type theories.
%%
%% For B(C)=c*(inputBits(C)+1)^d the original c,d remain fixed before all C.
%% The stopped executable reads only the original input, machine and budget;
%% it is not passed a proof of the Negative(C) promise. Promise coverage and
%% sound source readback prove correctness of the deadline interpretation.
%% An arbitrary timeout without that coverage still gives Unknown.
%%
%% 4. H24 POLYNOMIAL CLOSURE AND THE REMAINING INPUT
%%
%% Given original-size bounds
%%
%%   Phi(initial C) <= k*(N+1)^e,
%%   credit(initial C) <= b*(N+1)^f,
%%
%% the natural constructor returns the explicit envelope
%%
%%   actual_work <= (k+b)*(N+1)^max(e,f).
%%
%% The earlier paid-pipeline theorem composes this with the supplied local
%% producer/compiler/checker/readback/communication/control costs. The archive
%% also constructs polynomial sum, product and substitution bounds. These are
%% the cost rules used in the composite, not a claim that arbitrary coefficient
%% acquisition, a matrix operation at unbounded precision, or proof search has
%% unit bit cost.
%%
%% The uploaded archive supplies these bridge constructors. It does not supply
%% an all-CNF inhabitant giving the original fixed implementation, primitive
%% realization, local account and uniform initial bounds for every input in
%% that family. Its deadline/reserve equivalence gives two interchangeable
%% forms of that remaining source judgement. Replacing one by the other does
%% not itself discharge it. No new RH/GRH analytic target proof is asserted by
%% these clock and chart proofs; the earlier target definitions and statuses
%% are retained exactly.
%%
%% 5. DEDUPLICATION OF THE ORIGINAL MATRIX AND NORMALIZER
%%
%% The submitted six-coordinate sparse matrix is exactly the existing
%% pn25ArchivedMatrix. With T=pn25Change and S=pn25ChangeInverse,
%%
%%   rho(v)=T*pn25NativeMatrix(v)*S,     TS=ST=I,
%%   G=S^T*Q*S.
%%
%% Both matrices of the basis change are integral with determinant +/-1.
%% The outer 2x2 identity is
%%
%%   [[1,1],[0,1]] [[t-2b,0],[b,t]] [[1,-1],[0,1]]
%%        = [[t-b,b],[b,t-b]].
%%
%% There is no division by two. The uploaded Gram has determinant 3, and only
%% the central odd unit 3 is needed for its inverse. The new UB26 adapter
%% identifies its dagger with the atlas's existing pn25Gram.
%%
%% The submitted normal(A)=-(A+2*A^dagger)/3 is the existing pn25DaggerInverse;
%% inverse_normal(A)=A-2*A^dagger is pn25DaggerLinear. The proof identifiers
%% pn25_native_gram_square, pn25_same_native_dagger_chart and
%% pn25_original_dagger_resolvent_both_returns are reused.
%%
%% Independent native proofs now establish G and its inverse numerator's
%% symmetry, both inverse products, and the full six-formal-variable identity
%%
%%   GI3*rho(v)^T*G = rho(D*v),        D=3J,
%%   D^2=9I,
%%   (3I-2D)(-3I-2D)=(-3I-2D)(3I-2D)=27I.
%%
%% Dividing by central units 3 and 9 gives the same R,N mutual inverses. The
%% proofs concern complete integer coefficient arrays, not sampled assignments.
%% Agda uses dimension-indexed vectors; Lean uses independent finite lists and
%% shape proofs. Specializing coefficients to a ring with 3 invertible gives
%% the universal algebraic interpretation. The chart_alignment.py calculation
%% also reads the existing atlas definitions and the upload's G/GI3 directly,
%% and records their exact symbolic agreement.
%%
%% The six-channel cyclic normalizer, Gram dagger, transported sign involution,
%% and categorical family adjoints retain their distinct operations and types.
%% Shared return laws factor their proofs without identifying the operations.
%%
%% 6. MARKED CHARTS, CANONICITY AND NATURALITY
%%
%% The only section premise for arbitrary split charts is D_i E_i=1. Define
%%
%%   P_i=E_i D_i,   U_ji=E_j D_i,
%%   L_ji(a)=E_j a D_i.
%%
%% The single middle cancellation proves
%%
%%   L_kj(b)L_ji(a)=E_k b(D_j E_j)a D_i=L_ki(ba).
%%
%% Consequences include cocycle composition, image projectors, covariance,
%% source readback, and fusion of intermediate chart conversions. If D_i is
%% E_i's dagger, it also gives U_ji^dagger=U_ij and self-adjoint projectors.
%% For a self-adjoint source involution K,
%%
%%   F_i=E_i K D_i,    F_i^dagger=F_i,    F_i^2=P_i,
%%   U_ji F_i=F_j U_ji,                 F_i^(2n+1)=F_i.
%%
%% The odd-power identity is proved by native induction for every n. The
%% ambient identity is not substituted for the image projector. If N,R are
%% source inverses, their transported composition is P_i and hence returns
%% the original value on the admitted image.
%%
%% For the upload's concrete matrices, R^3=I, H^9=I and H^3!=I. There are nine
%% distinct embedding matrices E_i and three distinct rank-four images in
%% dimension twelve. Specifically E_(i+3)=E_i R, D_(i+3)=R^2 D_i, while P_i
%% and F_i repeat every three. The index remains retained data in a marked
%% pair (i,value), even when images agree.
%%
%% Canonicity here is constructive source canonicity: D_i(E_i p)=p for the
%% same retained p. It gives D_i(E_i p)=D_j(E_j p), without requiring two
%% independently found proof witnesses of the same proposition to be equal.
%% For an actual H24 build, p is literally build(policy,judgement). Both
%% encodings return that same term, with its original context.
%%
%% The existing comorphism contracts retain their satisfaction/decoder fields.
%% The family construction Sigma_f |- Delta_f |- Pi_f retains its supplied
%% fibre indices and witnesses. The new marked-source and clock families
%% compose pointwise with those already checked interfaces; a source context
%% is transformed only by its explicit map, never silently removed. The
%% existing triple-adjoint proofs and their evidence remain in the prior
%% contained archive; this continuation does not count them as new results.
%%
%% 7. ORDERED CONTEXTUAL CLOCK AND TROPICAL ACCOUNTS
%%
%% For contextual operators P,W use the upper block
%%
%%   C(P,W)=[[P,W],[0,P]].
%%
%% Both native systems construct
%%
%%   C(Q,Z)C(P,W)=C(QP,QW+ZP),
%%
%% its associative composition, identity and exact source decoder. No
%% commutativity of operators is used; the native interface does not even
%% require additive commutativity for this calculation. Hets imports only
%% the existing additive group and adds ordered multiplication, never the
%% atlas's commutative scalar-ring axiom for contextual operators.
%%
%% On basis states, P_f(e_x)=e_f(x), W_f,c(e_x)=c(x)e_f(x). The same ordered
%% product becomes
%%
%%   C(g,d) C(f,c)=C(g composed f, c+d composed f).
%%
%% This is state-dependent paid work. Reversing a paid event returns state
%% while keeping its cost; an event followed by its inverse contributes the
%% two positive costs. It does not become a zero-time identity.
%%
%% The retained natural slice K(n)=C(1,n) obeys K(n)K(m)=K(n+m). Reflection of
%% the original integer is conditional only on its faithful natural embedding.
%% A residue modulo 2^k alone wraps and cannot carry that reflection.
%%
%% The separate potential reweighting w'=w+phi(target)-phi(source) telescopes
%% to the endpoint difference. Closed walks keep total charge and comparisons
%% between common endpoints are preserved when the order is translation
%% invariant. In the nine-cycle example the reweighted list is
%% [5,10,5,10,5,10,5,5,8], with total 63. These supplied charge weights are
%% not the machine's paid bit work: that phi alone fails the first required
%% paid-credit inequality. The frontier account supplies the missing local
%% accounting data when available.
%%
%% Tropical values remain observations with declared laws. Entrywise matrix
%% valuation is submultiplicative in the appropriate valuation direction;
%% scalar marked coefficients may carry exact grades. In particular the
%% clause anchor has outer unit entries, so its FULL matrix valuation is zero.
%% Its grade is read from the designated middle coefficient. At precision k,
%% the branches 2^a,2^b return min(a,k),min(b,k). This preserves the actual
%% specified branch computation without assuming an assignment-global minimum.
%%
%% 8. ALL-PRECISION CHART INVERSION AND PHYSICS IDENTITIES
%%
%% The involution notes prove directly from the series that both submitted
%% charts F=tau and F=M have F(A)=A+4h(A) with h integral and 1-Lipschitz.
%% The constructive correction X_0=Y, X_(s+1)=Y+X_s-F(X_s) gains two dyadic
%% digits per step. Its finite inverses are coherent under reduction and
%% therefore assemble into the inverse limit. These are written all-precision
%% derivations, distinct from the finite uploaded tests and from the native
%% integer coefficient proofs. The two scripts' odd-polylog denominators
%% have exponents 2 and 1 respectively; they are kept parameter-distinct.
%%
%% The Landen identity gives M(-A)=-M(A)-8*ell(A)^2, and hence the returned
%% involution is M composed negation composed M^-1. The guard digit computes
%% at k+1 before dividing an even displacement by two, returning its k-bit
%% half-defect without inventing a dyadic inverse of two. Reflection and clause
%% decoder formulas, their isometry proofs and grade restrictions are given
%% in documentation/involution_proofs.txt.
%%
%% The exact Maxwell directional-symbol calculation gives A_v^3=|v|^2 A_v.
%% At unit v its square is the transverse projector. The full energy identity
%% is
%%
%%   |e|^2+|B|^2-2 v dot (e cross B)
%%     = |B-v cross e|^2+(v dot e)^2+(1-|v|^2)|e|^2.
%%
%% The final term vanishes for unit v. This polynomial identity and the
%% concrete nine-chart matrices have exact symbolic receipts and written
%% derivations; the generic categorical transport is independently native
%% checked. A physical runtime conclusion still uses its explicit primitive
%% cost and implementation account.
%%
%% 9. A PROVED CALCULATION SAVING IN THE UPLOADED INVERSE
%%
%% For F=Id+4h above, let r_s=Y-F(X_s). The exact residual identity is
%%
%%   r_0=-4h(Y),
%%   r_(s+1)=4*(h(X_s)-h(X_s+r_s)).
%%
%% It proves v(r_s)>=2(s+1). Therefore at precision k>=1, only
%%
%%   floor((k-1)/2)=ceil(k/2)-1
%%
%% updates are required. The original final update adds a zero residual modulo
%% 2^k. A separate optimized copy retains all source formulas, series bounds,
%% odd denominators and the k+1 guard digit. It changes only this loop count
%% and the output receipt name; the uploaded source is retained unchanged.
%%
%% All original assertions and seven counters passed with the shorter loop.
%% Its 3,143 inverse calls used 30,146 chart evaluations instead of the 33,289
%% required by the original bound on those same calls. The exact reduction is
%% 3,143 chart evaluations plus 3,143 matrix subtractions and additions each.
%% These are counted operations, not a host-time or all-problem complexity claim.
%%
%% For this iteration, the uniform bound is sharp in the stated class:
%% F(x)=5x, Y=1 has r_s=(-4)^(s+1). It is a worst-case statement about that
%% displayed constructor, not optimality over every inversion algorithm or a
%% specific lower bound for tau/M. This is the local H24 simplification used
%% here: retain the original return and remove a provably redundant paid step.
%%
%% 10. HOW TO REPLAY
%%
%% Extract the Python block BEGIN_H24_UPLOADED_BRIDGE_EXTRACT_PY from this
%% file, remove the leading Hets comment marker on each line, and run it with
%% this atlas and an output directory. It resolves content hashes across the
%% contained archives, verifies every body, and prevents escaping paths.
%%
%%   python extract_bridge.py Number_Theory_Torser_Atlas.het extracted
%%   python extracted/dual_gate.py --agda /path/to/agda --lean /path/to/lean
%%
%% The runtimes are actual installed Agda 2.9.0 and Lean 4.19.0 in this run;
%% their executables are not embedded. No old compiled proof objects are
%% required. The original signed-Int archive path remains available with its
%% reported propext/Quot.sound dependencies; the natural frontier closure used
%% by the strict gate is an unchanged-block extraction with a source map.
%%
%% checks/replay_calculations.py executes the preserved finite checkers and
%% the exact source-bound chart alignment; SymPy is needed for the symbolic
%% parts. Numerical tests are never converted into universal native receipts.
%% The Hets %implied clauses are proof obligations with named source/native
%% correspondences. A successful Hets static analysis means parsing and typing,
%% not that every %implied clause in the entire atlas was discharged by an ATP.
%%
%% All earlier formulas and their quantifier binders are preserved. New source
%% aliases and adapters keep one foundational definition for each original
%% object. The new manifest records native checks, symbolic computations,
%% written derivations, source parameters and preserved older goals separately.
%% END_H24_UPLOADED_BRIDGE_GUIDE

